{
  "work_package_id": "WP-003",
  "work_package_file": "work/WP-004.md",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "assigned_to": "QA",
  "dependencies": [
    "WP-001"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "Freeform search input filters the project list in real-time by matching against project name, ID, and description (case-insensitive substring match).",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Repository filter dropdown filters the project list to only projects containing the selected repository.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Sort selector toggles between alphabetical (name ascending, case-insensitive; tiebreaker: project ID ascending) and last-activity (descending; null/undefined LastActivity sorts last; tiebreaker: name ascending).",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Clearing all filters (empty search, \"All repositories\", any sort order) restores the full project list.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "An empty-state message \"No projects match the current filters.\" is displayed when filter criteria yield zero results.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "After creating a new project, all project data is re-fetched from the API and the current filter/sort state is re-applied.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "DOM clearing uses clearElement() from utils/dom.js — no innerHTML = '' for container clearing.",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-04-23T08:55:28Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-04-23T08:59:17Z",
      "duration_ms": 229000,
      "summary": [
        "Added module-level `_allProjects` cache array to dashboard.js — stores enriched project data (fullProject + wsCount) after each API fetch.",
        "Implemented `applyFiltersAndSort(filterState)` — applies search (case-insensitive substring on name/ID/description), repo filter (project must contain the selected repo ID), and sort (alpha: name asc + ID tiebreaker; activity: desc timestamp, null last, name tiebreaker).",
        "Implemented `renderProjectGrid(listContainer, filtered)` — renders cards or the appropriate empty-state message using clearElement(); distinguishes 'no projects at all' from 'filters excluded everything'.",
        "Refactored `renderProjectList(listContainer, filterState)` — now accepts filterState, populates `_allProjects`, then calls applyFiltersAndSort + renderProjectGrid.",
        "Wired `onFilterChange` in renderDashboard to call applyFiltersAndSort + renderProjectGrid (no re-fetch on filter change).",
        "Updated create-project `onSuccess` handler to call `renderProjectList(listContainer, filterState)` so data is re-fetched from the API and the current filter/sort state is re-applied.",
        "All AC7 container-clearing uses clearElement() — no innerHTML = '' introduced.",
        "Added gui/public/js/views/dashboard.test.mjs with 14 tests covering all 7 acceptance criteria. All 14 new tests + 100 pre-existing GUI tests pass (114 total)."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "gui/public/js/views/dashboard.js",
          "gui/public/js/views/dashboard.test.mjs"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-23T08:59:17Z",
          "note": "dashboard.js uses `innerHTML` in the `showLoading()` helper (line ~141) to inject the loading skeleton. This is a pre-existing pattern predating WP-001. Consider refactoring showLoading() to build the DOM imperatively using createElement + clearElement() for consistency with the rest of the module."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-23T08:59:17Z",
          "note": "`applyFiltersAndSort()` reads the `_allProjects` module-level variable implicitly. Making it a pure function (accepting `allProjects` as a parameter) would improve testability and make the data flow explicit. Currently testable only through the rendered DOM."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-23T08:59:17Z",
          "note": "The `alpha` sort comparator in `applyFiltersAndSort()` uses explicit `<`/`>` string comparisons rather than `String.prototype.localeCompare()`, which is inconsistent with the activity sort's tiebreaker that uses `localeCompare`. Unifying to `localeCompare` throughout would improve locale-correctness consistency."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-04-23T08:59:59Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-04-23T09:02:12Z",
      "duration_ms": 133000,
      "summary": [
        "All 7 acceptance criteria verified via the 14-test suite (14/14 PASS). Full regression run of 114 GUI tests (all PASS, 0 failures). Four edge-case stress tests all passed: (1) debounce fires only on the last keypress after rapid input; (2) projects with an empty Repositories array do not crash the repo filter and correctly show the empty-state; (3) 500-project list renders without errors in ~196ms; (4) source scan confirms no innerHTML='' container-clearing pattern in dashboard.js."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "14 AC-targeted tests + 100 pre-existing regression tests",
        "tests_passed": 114,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-23T09:02:12Z",
          "note": "applyFiltersAndSort() closes over _allProjects implicitly. The Developer flagged this as a testability debt — currently only testable through the rendered DOM. Low priority since the 14 existing tests provide adequate coverage, but worth tracking for a future refactor."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-23T09:02:12Z",
          "note": "Alpha sort uses explicit `<`/`>` comparisons while activity sort tiebreaker uses localeCompare(). Inconsistency pre-flagged by Developer. No AC violation, but a locale-correctness improvement opportunity."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-23T09:02:12Z",
          "note": "Edge-case verified: projects with empty Repositories array correctly trigger the empty-state when a repo filter is applied — no runtime crash."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-23T09:02:12Z",
          "note": "Debounce timing verified: 5 rapid keystrokes at 20ms intervals (well within the 250ms window) fire only one filter evaluation reflecting the final input value."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-04-23T08:55:28Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-04-23T09:02:12Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-23T08:59:17Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 7 acceptance criteria are implemented and verified by 14 passing unit tests. Key behaviours to validate during QA: (1) search debounce fires at ~250ms; (2) repo filter only shows projects whose Repositories array contains the matching repo ID; (3) activity sort places null LastActivity entries last with a name tiebreaker; (4) the create-project form's onSuccess re-fetches from the API (not just re-filters cached data); (5) clearElement() is used for all container clearing — no innerHTML = '' regressions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-23T09:02:12Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 7 ACs are met and verified by 14 passing unit tests + 114 total GUI tests (0 failures). Key implementation details for code review: (1) applyFiltersAndSort() reads _allProjects as a module-level closure — consider whether this is acceptable or should be refactored to a pure function; (2) alpha sort uses explicit string comparisons rather than localeCompare — low-risk inconsistency worth noting; (3) showLoading() helper uses innerHTML assignment for the loading skeleton (pre-existing, not introduced by this WP, not an AC7 violation). No blocking issues found."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

